{"duration_api_ms":215968,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"c19c030f-ce1d-4010-ad9e-0e0feceb2c74","total_cost_usd":0.265884,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15630,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":20336,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":14734},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15630,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":20336,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15630,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15630},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":20336,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":15630,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.265884,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":14734,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"observation\":\"The feasible front is a one-dimensional curve traced by flight-path angle at D~3.375-3.38 m, bluntness 1.2, cone 70 deg (the variable upper bounds). Flux runs 228k to 275k W/m2 and bondline T runs 418 to 391 K. Two hard limits bind: heatshield mass fraction and max_g. Mass-fraction margin scales as D^2 and does not depend on b, cone or gamma. Margin is 0.006044 at D=3.375, 0.0207 at 3.35 and 0.0013 at 3.383, which puts the ceiling near D=3.385. Peak g depends almost only on gamma (about 1.7 g/deg near -3.56), with a weak rise with D (about 0.43 g/m). It hits 12 g at about gamma=-3.57. Larger D lowers both flux (about -119k W/m2 per m) and T (about -18 K/m). Lower b is worse on both objectives. Bluntness 1.205 and above at cone 70 fails the cd_fore convex-hull check, and b>=1.3 gives invalid geometry. So the remaining gains are pushing D to the mass-fraction ceiling, pushing gamma to the g limit, and filling the front. I also run a few probes of b and cone below their bounds.\",\"evidence\":[\"C-e6bfb3db2b24, C-465478728e6f, C-799a5eaff9e3, C-4749105a6ed4 and C-f3e186a3d6a9: mass margin follows 0.99396*(D/3.375)^2. Ceiling is D~3.385.\",\"C-e6bfb3db2b24 and C-4749105a6ed4: g is 11.981 at (3.38, -3.56) and 11.982 at (3.35, -3.568), so g barely depends on D. g reaches 12 at about gamma=-3.57.\",\"C-72093e041d67 to C-f3e186a3d6a9: T falls about 11 K/deg and flux rises about 24k W/m2 per deg as gamma steepens.\",\"C-4749105a6ed4 vs C-e6bfb3db2b24: smaller D raises both flux and T, so D at its cap is best.\",\"C-d4ad05ba9bb6 vs C-f3e186a3d6a9: b=1.19 is slightly worse than b=1.2 on both objectives.\",\"C-207a027e9dd5, C-4d9cd4c2b38d, C-1b507004c89c and C-de929f2046c9: b>=1.205 at cone 70 fails the cd_fore hull check.\",\"C-f986776067bd, C-9c1cc1a27672, C-e88bc745fe3b and C-51a1525266f1: cone too small for the given b makes the geometry invalid.\",\"C-114b79b08144 (3.2, 1.1, 69, -3.7) has T 393.8 K and flux 307k, worse than the extrapolated D~3.38 line. This confirms that lower D and b are worse.\"],\"mechanism\":\"Stagnation heating falls with nose radius (b*D/2) and with lower ballistic coefficient (larger D), so D and b are best at their caps. Bondline temperature follows heat load, which drops for steeper, shorter pulses. Peak g is set mainly by gamma, so the front is traced by gamma up to the g=12 limit. The D cap comes from mass fraction, which scales with D^2. Moving D from 3.375 to 3.384 lowers flux by about 1.1k W/m2 and T by about 0.16 K at every gamma. This shifts the whole front down slightly. The front is convex, so the intermediate gammas add small hypervolume. Probes at b<1.2 and cone<70 check whether any lever beyond this 1-D curve exists. I expect them to be dominated (this relies partly on prior physical reasoning, since the data only covers b=1.1 at cone 69).\",\"uncertainty\":\"The g margin near gamma=-3.57 is only about 0.0003 at D=3.384, so the boundary probes may be infeasible. The mass-fraction ceiling at D=3.385 leaves a 0.00014 margin and depends on my D^2 fit. The b and cone probes may hit an extrapolation or geometry failure, since the cd_fore hull boundary and the overlap boundary are not mapped. Flux and T predictions come from linear interpolation and scaling of the D=3.375 line, with errors of a few hundred W/m2 and a few tenths of a K.\",\"proposals\":[{\"parent_id\":\"C-8c34eb1f2d71\",\"rationale\":\"Left end of the front at the shallowest gamma, D raised to the mass-fraction cap. Dominates the current left-end point.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":227140,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":417.94,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Confirms the D scaling of flux and T at shallow gamma.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-bc819d1f4dc4\",\"rationale\":\"Same gamma as the front point at -1.75, with D at the cap.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":232170,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":413.87,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Shifts the front down and left.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-5d906bbb7e30\",\"rationale\":\"Same gamma as the front point at -2.0, with D at the cap.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":237550,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":410.03,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Shifts the front down and left.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-5d906bbb7e30\",\"rationale\":\"Fills the convex gap between gamma -1.75 and -2.0 at the D cap.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-1.9},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":235400,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":411.57,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds coverage on the convex front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-cdf8f3d62c9d\",\"rationale\":\"Intermediate gamma at the D cap between -2.25 and -2.5.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.3},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":244350,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":405.77,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds coverage in the mid-left of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-20662a735ab5\",\"rationale\":\"Same gamma as the front point at -2.5, with D at the cap.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":249010,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":403.08,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Shifts the front down and left.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-74069e8a9a84\",\"rationale\":\"Intermediate gamma -2.7 at the D cap.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-2.7},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":253740,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":400.57,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds coverage in the middle of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-1e1903a70eaf\",\"rationale\":\"Intermediate gamma -3.0 at the D cap.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.0},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":260920,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":397.04,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds coverage in the middle of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-866a02f94e0b\",\"rationale\":\"Same gamma as the front point at -3.1, with D at the cap.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":263330,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":395.92,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Shifts the front down and left.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-23afbf9fd8ba\",\"rationale\":\"Intermediate gamma -3.35 at the D cap. g is about 11.65 here, so it is safely feasible.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.35},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":269390,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.29,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds coverage in the right part of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-72093e041d67\",\"rationale\":\"Same gamma as the front point at -3.45, with D at the cap.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":271800,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.27,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Shifts the front down and left.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-72093e041d67\",\"rationale\":\"Gamma -3.5 at the D cap, filling the gap between -3.45 and -3.55.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":273020,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.79,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds coverage near the low-T end.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e6bfb3db2b24\",\"rationale\":\"D near its cap and gamma just inside the g limit. Predicted g is about 11.996.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.568},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274640,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.11,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Pushes the lowest-T corner of the front.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e6bfb3db2b24\",\"rationale\":\"Probes the mass-fraction ceiling (D=3.385, margin about 0.00014) with gamma -3.566 (g about 11.993).\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.385,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.566},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274470,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.11,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests whether the D^2 mass-fraction fit holds up to the ceiling.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e6bfb3db2b24\",\"rationale\":\"Boundary probe at gamma -3.57. g is predicted at about 12.000, so this sits right on the limit and may be infeasible.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.57},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274690,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.09,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Locates the g=12 boundary precisely, at the cost of one possible infeasible slot.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e6bfb3db2b24\",\"rationale\":\"Gamma -3.55 at D 3.384 gives a safer g margin (about 11.96) and adds a point next to the low-T end.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.55},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274200,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":391.31,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Robust feasible point near the low-T end.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-72093e041d67\",\"rationale\":\"Gamma -3.4 at the D cap, filling the gap between -3.3 and -3.45.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.4},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":270590,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.78,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"low\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Adds coverage and refines the convex front near the right end.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e6bfb3db2b24\",\"rationale\":\"Probe cone 69.5 at b=1.2, D at the cap, gamma -3.5. Checks whether the cone bound is optimal and whether the hull and geometry allow it.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.5,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":274000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.0,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Tests sensitivity to cone angle; no cone variation at b=1.2 has been tried.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e6bfb3db2b24\",\"rationale\":\"Probe b=1.1 at cone 70. Prior data suggests lower b is worse; this quantifies the b-sensitivity with the other variables held.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.1,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":279000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.7,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"medium\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Cleanly separates the b effect from the D and cone effects seen in C-114b79b08144.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e6bfb3db2b24\",\"rationale\":\"Probe b=1.0 at cone 68 to map the lower-b geometry and hull region.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.0,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":68.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":283000,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":393.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Maps the b and cone landscape away from the corner, in case a different optimum exists.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0},{\"parent_id\":\"C-e6bfb3db2b24\",\"rationale\":\"Probe b=1.15 at cone 69, which is within the valid geometry seen at b=1.1 with cone 69.\",\"parameter_changes\":{\"diameter_m\":3.384,\"bluntness_ratio\":1.15,\"cone_half_angle_deg\":69.0,\"flight_path_angle_deg\":-3.5},\"expected_outcome\":{\"peak_heat_flux_w_m2\":276500,\"peak_bondline_temperature_k\":392.3,\"feasible\":true},\"uncertainty\":\"high\",\"reason_to_simulate\":\"Checks whether trading b for cone angle helps, and whether this point is valid.\",\"requested_fidelity\":0}]}","ttft_ms":171745,"type":"result","duration_ms":216009,"uuid":"0498a031-5ec1-4a85-ba2a-adb277120b5f","ttft_stream_ms":1553,"time_to_request_ms":40,"first_content_frame_ms":1553,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
